# POLLY, songcopy: Copy song gives the target four patterns of its own, never one the source plays. Song 1
# plays P01 (a note recorded), P02, P03 and, as its Ending, P06 (a copy of P01): song 2's own P06 is the
# source's, so its Main B gets a free one (P04); P06 keeps its note. A flash error leaves the song unchanged.
wait 300
tap LFO
spin K1 2
wait 100
expect song_bars 1
tap HOME
tap PLAY
tap REC
tapkey 7
wait 600
tap REC
tap PLAY
wait 100
tap SAVE
wait 50
expect pat0_nev 1
# P01 copied to P06 (the pattern's jobs), and P06 made song 1's Ending
tap SEQ
press SAVE
wait 800
release SAVE
spin K1 1
spin K2 4
tap SEL
wait 50
expect pat5_nev 1
tap ENV
tap ENV
expect page 9
spin K4 2
wait 50
expect song1_style3 5
# Copy song 1 to song 2
press SAVE
wait 800
release SAVE
expect job 2
spin K1 1
tap SEL
wait 50
shot copied.png
expect song2_bars 1
expect song2_style0 4
expect song2_style1 3
expect song2_style2 6
expect song2_style3 7
expect pat5_nev 1
expect pat4_nev 1
expect pat7_nev 1
# a flash error while copying to song 3: the song stays as it was
flash_fail 1
press SAVE
wait 800
release SAVE
spin K1 1
spin K2 1
tap SEL
wait 50
shot flash_error.png
expect song3_bars 0
flash_fail 0
